tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="center">HIV-1</td><td align="center">non-engineered</td><td align="center">45 (1460)</td><td align="center">59 (340)</td><td align="center">0.8</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="center">HIV-1</td><td align="center">B7+antiCD3</td><td align="center">49 (1100)</td><td align="center">54 (225)</td><td align="center">0.9</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup>1</sup>Data from Donor-L cells</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec><sec><title>Induction of specific antibody responses</title><p>Unlike HIV-1, HSV-2 does not replicate in PBLs and replication inhibition assays could not be done. In order to demonstrate HSV specific responses, humoral immune response experiments were performed (Table <xref ref-type="table" rid="T4">4</xref>, Expt. 1 and 2).</p><table-wrap position="float" id="T4"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Particle-induced Antibody Formation</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td></td><td align="center" colspan="2"><bold><underline>Particle Preparations</underline></bold></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="center"><bold>Expt.</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Virus</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Modification</bold></td><td align="center" colspan="9"><bold><underline>Relative Optical Density Units</underline></bold></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="center"><bold>1.</bold></td><td></td><td></td><td align="center" colspan="3"><bold>HSV-1 Coated</bold></td><td align="center" colspan="3"><bold>HSV-2 Coated</bold></td><td align="center" colspan="3"><bold>HIV-1 Coated</bold></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td colspan="9"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="center"><bold>9D</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>13D</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>16D</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>9D</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>13D</bold></td><td align=